{
  "info": {
    "name": "Demo-world matrix (SPA-CHALLENGE-UX - the console's supervised world)",
    "description": "The world scripts/postman/seed-demo-data.sh builds for the browser console, asserted through the gateway on EXACT ids: sup-demo supervises pm-demo, is bound to NO team, and therefore sees two catalogs purely by derivation - one tagged env=production, one untagged. Reading the production catalog's CONTENTS challenges her (RFC 9470); the same read by pm-demo, a MEMBER, does not. That asymmetry is the demo.\n\nThis is NOT a matrix in the usual sense: it owns no fixtures and tears nothing down. It asserts a SEEDED world (fixture family d311..., owned by seed-demo-data.sh), which is why it is safe to run beside every other matrix - and E32 proves exactly that in both directions.\n\nFOUR FOLDERS, run in order by run-demo-world-matrix.sh: 'Demo world' (E31a-h) on the freshly seeded rig; 'Idempotency' (E31i-j) after a SECOND seed run; 'Coexistence' (E32a-d) after the supervised-scope and step-up matrices have run; 'Convergence' (E33a-c) after a realm re-import plus a re-seed (the runner's --convergence mode).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gateway",
      "value": "http://localhost:9085"
    },
    {
      "key": "collection_base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:9085/api/v1"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Demo world",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "E31a \u2014 HEADLINE: sup-demo (bound to NO team) GET /catalogs -> exactly the two demo catalogs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{sup_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{collection_base_url}}/catalogs?perPage=50",
              "host": [
                "{{collection_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "catalogs"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "perPage",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('E31a 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const ids = body.items.map(i => i.id);",
                  "// sup-demo owns no seat anywhere: every row here is DERIVED from the single edge to pm-demo.",
                  "pm.test('E31a sup-demo sees EXACTLY 2 catalogs', () => pm.expect(body.count).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.test('E31a both demo catalogs are present, by exact id', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.environment.get('demo_prod_catalog_id'));",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.environment.get('demo_open_catalog_id'));",
                  "});",
                  "// The flagship Demo catalog is governed by a team sup-demo has nothing to do with: it must NOT leak.",
                  "pm.test('E31a the flagship demo catalog is NOT in her page', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.not.include(pm.environment.get('demo_catalog_id')));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('observed_sup_ids', JSON.stringify(ids.slice().sort()));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "E31b \u2014 the tier states: production tagged, open untagged",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{sup_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{collection_base_url}}/catalogs?perPage=50",
              "host": [
                "{{collection_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "catalogs"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "perPage",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('E31b 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const items = pm.response.json().items;",
                  "const prod = items.find(i => i.id === pm.environment.get('demo_prod_catalog_id'));",
                  "const open = items.find(i => i.id === pm.environment.get('demo_open_catalog_id'));",
                  "pm.test('E31b the production catalog carries env=production', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(prod, 'production catalog row').to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(prod.tags.env).to.eql('production');",
                  "});",
                  "// The open catalog is UNTAGGED on purpose - it is the no-ceremony control the console needs.",
                  "pm.test('E31b the open catalog carries NO env tag', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(open, 'open catalog row').to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(open.tags && open.tags.env).to.be.oneOf([undefined, null]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "E31c \u2014 no ceremony: sup-demo reads the OPEN catalog's contents at aal1",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{sup_token}}"
